# Agent workflow

When working on `agent/**` branches or issues labeled `agent`:

1. Read `docs/AGENT_RUNBOOK.md`, `docs/AGENT_CODING_STANDARDS.md`, `docs/AGENT_ISSUE_RESPONSE.md`, and `docs/AGENT_IDENTITY.md` first.
2. Branch: `agent/issue-<number>-<short-slug>`.
3. Every commit must include:
   `Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent <noreply@cursor.com>`
   Use `./scripts/agent-commit-msg.sh` or `source ./scripts/agent-git-env.sh && agent_commit`.
4. Validate before push: `./scripts/verify.sh --quality`
5. Push only; do not open PRs manually — **Agent Open PR** creates them.
6. Before merge: fill PR **What was fixed** and **User impact** (required for auto-merge). See `docs/AGENT_ISSUE_RESPONSE.md`.
7. Provider surface changes: follow `docs/AGENT_CODING_STANDARDS.md` (manifest, docs, examples, acceptance tests).
8. Do not merge, tag releases, or commit secrets. Pick up `regression`-labeled reopened issues like new work.

## Focused review lenses

**Every agent issue:** intake selects lenses automatically; Cloud Agent must append sweeps to `docs/reports/agent-review-log.md`. **Agent Validate** enforces the log update.

**Every release:** **Agent Release Orchestrate** → intake with release-tier lenses → **Agent Release Tag** when verdict clears (`docs/testing/release-lens-review.md`).

Human branches (`codex/*`, etc.) follow `CONTRIBUTING.md` and `docs/MAINTENANCE_PLAYBOOK.md`.
